0112:     - A color may contain more than one separated fragment; each fragment has at least two pixels.
0113:     - All completed copies fit inside the grid and do not overlap other foreground pixels.
0114: 
0115:     Rule
0116:     - Use the unique foreground color with the most pixels as the template mask.
0117:     - For each other color, find the unique minimum set of translated template placements whose existing template cells cover that color's input pixels.
0118:     - Paint every cell of those placements with that color, leaving the template and background otherwise unchanged.
0119: 
0120:     Key insight
0121:     The incomplete colors are partial masks of the same template; their existing pixels act as anchors that determine where the missing cells must be filled.
0122:     """
